This folder includes all scripts for transforming different datasets into the following format:
    1. In the format of .csv
    2. Every feature will be transformed into binary feature(using one-hot encoding)
    3. The name of binary feature will be printed in the first line of .csv file
        -> If there is not supported with the .name file, so just choosing the fi_j as the name, 
           where i is the index of feature, and j is the index of value in the one-hot encoding
        -> If there is supported .name file, so use the name_feature_j as the name

There are some pre-requirements for datasets:
    1. The last item of each record is the label of record
    2. The label of dataset must be binary
    3. In option, an .name file for describing the dataset is needed(same format for C4.5)
    4. Assume that all data have been changed into the integer format



